{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "Shared vectors for the Studio navigation domain allow-list (STUDIO-FLEX-001). Consumed by the backend AllowedDomains (Java) and by the studio-runner (TypeScript); a reference implementation runs in tools/check-studio-observed-contracts.cjs. Config keys: studio.navigation.allowed-domains / STUDIO_ALLOWED_DOMAINS (backend), STUDIO_RUNNER_ALLOWED_DOMAINS (runner). The allow-all option (STUDIO_ALLOW_ALL_DOMAINS / STUDIO_RUNNER_ALLOW_ALL_DOMAINS) is pinned by allowAllEnvCases and allowAllMatchCases.",
  "rules": [
    "Configuration entries. An entry is one host suffix: lowercase ASCII, punycode for internationalised names (xn--...), labels of 1-63 characters from a-z 0-9 and hyphen (no leading or trailing hyphen), 1-253 characters in total, and a last label that starts with a letter (so no IPv4 literal, no numeric host such as 127.1 and no hexadecimal form can be an entry). The regular expression in entryGrammar is normative.",
    "A configuration is a list of at most 32 entries. It is refused as a whole when any entry violates the grammar (this covers wildcards, IPv4/IPv6 literals, schemes, ports, paths, userinfo, whitespace, empty strings, leading/trailing/double dots, uppercase and non-punycode names) or when two entries overlap. Entries a and b overlap when a == b or a ends with \".\" + b or b ends with \".\" + a, so exactly one entry can match any host. The empty list is valid and denies everything. Entry order is irrelevant.",
    "Runner environment form (STUDIO_RUNNER_ALLOWED_DOMAINS). Unset or the empty string means the empty list. Any other value is split on \",\" with no trimming; every segment must be a valid entry (so \"a.com,\" and \"a.com, b.com\" are refused) and the resulting list must be valid as a whole.",
    "Candidate URL to host (hostOf). The result is the lowercase punycode host, or null, and null never matches. Steps in order: (1) null when the string contains a backslash, a space or any control character (U+0000-U+0020, U+007F). (2) The scheme must be http or https, case-insensitive, followed by \"://\"; anything else (about:, data:, javascript:, file:, blob:, ftp:, scheme-relative, \"http:/x\") is null. (3) The authority is the text up to the first \"/\", \"?\" or \"#\"; null when it is empty or contains \"@\" (userinfo), \"%\" or a bracket (IPv6 literal). (4) When the authority has a \":\", the part after the first \":\" must be 1-5 digits with a value from 1 to 65535, otherwise null; any port is accepted otherwise, and the scheme is not tied to a port. (5) The host part is converted with IDNA ToASCII (Java IDN.toASCII, Node domainToASCII) and lowercased; a conversion failure is null. (6) The converted host must satisfy entryGrammar; this makes a trailing dot, an empty label, an underscore, an IP literal and an over-long host null.",
    "Match. A candidate URL is allowed when hostOf(url) is not null and, for some entry, host == entry or host ends with \".\" + entry. Path, query and fragment are ignored. Matching is on label boundaries only: evilciti.com and citi.com.evil.com never match the entry citi.com.",
    "Allow-all option (STUDIO_ALLOW_ALL_DOMAINS on the backend, STUDIO_RUNNER_ALLOW_ALL_DOMAINS on the runner; one chart value renders both). ON by default for now (user decision 2026-10-25). Exactly \"true\" means on and exactly \"false\" means off; any other non-empty value (including TRUE, 1, yes and padded forms) is a configuration error that stops startup. Unset (and, on the runner, the empty string) takes the deployment default, which is ON for now; that default lives in a different place on each side (the backend application.yml placeholder, the runner parser) and the chart always renders an explicit value, so it is deliberately not a shared vector. Off changes nothing above. On, the configured list is ignored for matching (it is still validated as above, so a typo is not hidden) and a candidate URL is allowed exactly when hostOf(url) is not null: the same http(s) DNS-name rule, still no userinfo, no IP literal, no other scheme. See allowAllEnvCases and allowAllMatchCases.",
    "Consumers: backend AllowedDomains (Java) and the runner (TypeScript) both run every case; tools/check-studio-observed-contracts.cjs runs a reference implementation over this file. Cases avoid IDNA 2003/UTS 46 differences (no sharp s, no fullwidth forms, no ideographic full stop)."
  ],
  "entryGrammar": "^(?=.{1,253}$)(?:[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?\\.)*[a-z](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$",
  "limits": {
    "maxEntries": 32,
    "maxEntryLength": 253,
    "maxLabelLength": 63,
    "maxPort": 65535
  },
